#' phc_flair
#' @description NACCADRC ADSP PHC Imaging FLAIR dataset. All NACC FLAIR data processed through PHC (Contains  legacy/mixed protocol data, as well as SCAN-compliant data on ADRC participants funded through any mechanism, including P30 funds, CLARiTI funded, or other sources). The data is sourced from the file(s) NACC_ADSP_PHC_FLAIR_2026.02.18.csv. 
#' @format A data frame with 13104 rows and 24 variables:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{NACCID}{Subject ID ( Prefix ""NACC"" followed by six numbers)}
#'   \item{SUBJID}{ADSP Subject ID}
#'   \item{NACCVNUM}{Visit Number}
#'   \item{PHC_Visit}{Harmonized Visit Number}
#'   \item{PHC_Age_FLAIR}{Age at each FLAIR visit}
#'   \item{Internal_scanID}{Image scan ID}
#'   \item{Analysis_Year}{Year data was analyzed}
#'   \item{Data_Source}{Source of the downloaded data}
#'   \item{Analysis_Status}{Status of analysis change for data}
#'   \item{Scan_Date}{Date of Scan}
#'   \item{EchoTime}{Echo Time}
#'   \item{RepetitionTime}{Repetition Time}
#'   \item{FlipAngle}{Flip Angle}
#'   \item{FieldStrength}{Magnetic Field Strength}
#'   \item{Manufacturer}{MRI Manufacturer}
#'   \item{Model}{MRI Manufacturer Model Name}
#'   \item{Image_Dimensions_vox}{Dimensions of the acquired FLAIR image}
#'   \item{SliceThickness}{Resolution in the z direction}
#'   \item{CNR_WM}{Contrast-to-noise ratio for total white matter}
#'   \item{SNR_WM}{Signal-to-noise ratio for total white matter}
#'   \item{CNR_GM}{Contrast-to-noise ratio for total gray matter}
#'   \item{SNR_GM}{Signal-to-noise ratio for total gray matter}
#'   \item{Contrast_WM_GM}{Measure of the contrast difference between white matter and gray matter in the MRI scan.}
#'   \item{PHC_WMHVOL_Harmonized}{Total volume of white matter hyperintensities (WMH) in the brain, measured in cubic centimeters harmonized across studies using standard Combat method}
#' }
#' @docType data
#' @keywords datasets
#' @name phc_flair
#' @usage data(phc_flair)
#' @source \href{https://www.naccdata.org/about-nacc-data/}{https://www.naccdata.org/about-nacc-data/}.
#' @examples
